---
import Dev from '../layouts/Dev.astro';
import '../styles/artwork-gallery.css';
---
<Dev title="Screenshots">
  <h1>Screenshots</h1>
  <p>Original native captures, paired by page and state. A missing platform stays empty; another screen is never substituted.</p>
  <form class="gallery-filters" role="search" aria-label="Filter screenshots">
    <label>Page or state<input id="capture-search" type="search" placeholder="Wallet, model picker, receive..." /></label>
    <label>Freshness<select id="capture-status"><option value="">All statuses</option><option>current</option><option>outdated</option><option>unverified</option><option>unknown</option><option>notattempted</option><option>missing</option><option>withdrawn</option></select></label>
    <label>Capture attempt<select id="capture-attempt"><option value="">All attempts</option><option>planned</option><option>blocked</option><option>notattempted</option><option>running</option><option>failed</option><option>captured</option><option>verified</option><option>stale</option></select></label>
    <label class="dev-check"><input id="capture-drafts" type="checkbox" /> Preview outdated / unverified captures as drafts</label>
    <button id="catalog-refresh" type="button">Refresh sources</button>
  </form>
  <p id="catalog-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Reading registered captures...</p>
  <div id="capture-groups"></div>
  <p class="dev-note">Current means app-source matched, not native-build verified. Native-fixture captures show seeded presentation data; native-navigation captures show navigation on a disposable profile. Neither establishes functional results. Import eligibility is not publication review. Latest capture attempts are independent of retained image freshness. Draft filenames disclose their status; originals remain unmodified.</p>
  <noscript>This local catalog needs JavaScript. Run the site dev server to read registered sources.</noscript>
</Dev>
<script>
  import { mountScreenshots } from '../../scripts/catalog-browser.mjs';
  mountScreenshots();
</script>
